      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Knowing the hops pays off when something breaks, because each failure looks different. Can't resolve the name? That's DNS."
        },
        {
          "text": "A connection that times out never reached Traefik: a node is down, or its ServiceLB pod is."
        },
        {
          "text": "A certificate error is TLS: check the Certificate, and whether the laptop trusts the company root."
        },
        {
          "text": "Traefik's plain 404 means no route: either no rule matches, or the Service has no ready pods. Episodes 5 and 6."
        },
        {
          "text": "401 or 403 comes from the app, about the token."
        },
        {
          "text": "And the app's own 404 page means every hop worked. There's just no link by that name yet.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
